%N A277829 First Series of Hankel determinants based on squares of Catalan numbers.
%C A277829 It would be very useful to have the formula for this sequence.
%H A277829 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A277829/b277829.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..41</a>
%H A277829 Wenlin Zhang and Haobo Ma, <a href="https://the-omega-institute.github.io/trureturing-mdbook/Problems/oeis-a277829-a278770-catalan-square-hankel-limits.html">A277829 and A278770: squared-Catalan Hankel limits</a>, 2026.
%H A277829 Wenlin Zhang and Haobo Ma, <a href="/A277829/a277829.pdf">Shift asymptotics for squared-Catalan Hankel determinants</a>, Oct 01 2026
%F A277829 Conjecture: lim n->infinity log(a(n))/n^2 = 2*log(2). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 29 2016 [Proved in the paper by Wenlin Zhang and Haobo Ma, Oct 01 2026]
%F A277829 Limit_{n->oo} (a(n)/4^(n^2))^(1/n) = exp(J)/32, where J = (1/Pi) * Integral_{0..Pi} log(2F1(3/2,3/2;3;cos^2(theta/2))) dtheta. [Wenlin Zhang and Haobo Ma, Oct 01 2026]
%p A277829 a:= n-> LinearAlgebra[Determinant](Matrix(n, (i, j)->
%p A277829         (t-> (binomial(2*t, t)/(t+1))^2)(i+j-1))):
%p A277829 seq(a(n), n=0..15);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Nov 28 2016
%t A277829 Flatten[{1, Table[Det[Table[(CatalanNumber[i + j - 1])^2, {i, n}, {j, n}]], {n,
%t A277829   11}]}]
%Y A277829 Cf. A000108, A278770.
%K A277829 nonn,changed
%O A277829 0,3
